Anthony,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on lodges, re=
serves and farms; we don't sell packages.

On a Big 5 reserve the network carries more than guest Wi-Fi: rangers
and guides in the field, gates and cameras, and the payments behind the
lodge. When that rides on rented links and whatever signal reaches the
lodge, the gaps show up exactly where incidents happen. I've copied Amelia
as GM.

I'd like to run a desk study on Garden Route Game Lodge from terrain and publ=
ic
infrastructure data first: where a backbone can run across the reserve and
how a reliable uplink gets onto it. It tells you what is feasible before
anyone spends money.

If that's useful, the next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you
have, what fails, what it costs you, and what an owned network would look
like. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and the report is yours
either way. The one-page proposal is attached; the short version is here:
www.cttx.co.za/assessment

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

